      "slug": "trametes-versicolor",
      "commonName": "turkey-tail",
      "scientificName": "Trametes versicolor",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/160331738/medium.jpg",
      "distinction": "Turkey-tail differs from its Trametes relatives by having the most variable and vibrant color patterns - while Northern Cinnabar Polypore is distinctly reddish-orange and Hairy Bracket is notably fuzzy, turkey-tail displays the widest range of colors in distinct concentric bands."
    },
    {
      "slug": "trametes-cinnabarina",
      "commonName": "Northern Cinnabar Polypore",
      "scientificName": "Trametes cinnabarina",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/161138523/medium.jpg",
      "distinction": "Within the Trametes genus, this species stands out for its solid, brilliant orange color without the multicolored bands typical of Turkey-tail or the white/cream colors of many other relatives."
    },
    {
      "slug": "trametes-betulina",
      "commonName": "Gilled Polypore",
      "scientificName": "Trametes betulina",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/335404742/medium.jpg",
      "distinction": "Among its Trametes relatives, Gilled Polypore is instantly distinguished by having true gills instead of the pores found in Turkey-tail or the maze-like patterns of White Maze Polypore."
    },
    {
      "slug": "trametes-gibbosa",
      "commonName": "Lumpy Bracket",
      "scientificName": "Trametes gibbosa",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/34683955/medium.jpg",
      "distinction": "Unlike the smooth, velvety turkey-tail with its colorful concentric zones, lumpy bracket is much plainer and bumpier."
    },
    {
      "slug": "trametes-conchifer",
      "commonName": "little nest polypore",
      "scientificName": "Trametes conchifer",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/106187671/medium.jpg",
      "distinction": "Unlike its Trametes relatives like turkey-tail which form flat, colorfully zoned shelves, the little nest polypore is immediately recognizable by its unique cup shape."
    },
    {
      "slug": "trametes-hirsuta",
      "commonName": "Hairy Bracket",
      "scientificName": "Trametes hirsuta",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/113603380/medium.jpeg",
      "distinction": "Among its Trametes relatives, Hairy Bracket stands out for its distinctly fuzzy upper surface - most other species in this genus like Turkey-tail and Cinnabar Bracket have smooth, almost glossy caps."
    },
    {
